New docint.spec.ts case, placed directly after the case that ends by asserting status 'reviewed':
- re-reads the document and asserts it is still 'reviewed';
- POSTs /docint/documents/${docId}/review with a fresh sessionId and idempotencyKey;
- asserts 409 and a message containing 'can be reviewed';
- asserts there is no review_sessions row for the refused id.

It fails with the guard commented out (the machine's TransitionError message) and passes with the new guard. The client's literal table lives only in the test.

